Subject: [PATCH 07447/11362] [outer-loop] REQ-PUBLISH-042: switch to
 ERNIE-Image-Turbo (8 steps), disable prompt enhancer

Two same-day follow-up revisions to the local paperbanana diagram-generation
backend, both grounded in real verification rather than assumption:

1. Model swap: baidu/ERNIE-Image (50 steps, guidance_scale=4.0) ->
   baidu/ERNIE-Image-Turbo (8 steps, guidance_scale=1.0), per user directive.
   guidance_scale=1.0 is load-bearing, not cosmetic -- confirmed via the
   Turbo model's own HuggingFace card that its DMD+RL distillation target
   bakes in classifier-free guidance differently from the base model, so
   reusing guidance_scale=4.0 would likely degrade output, not just run
   slower. Also switched the loader from the generic
   diffusers.DiffusionPipeline to the specific diffusers.ErnieImagePipeline
   class the Turbo model card's own example uses (confirmed it exists in
   this project's installed diffusers==0.39.0 first). Re-verified
   external/paperbanana is still at latest git tag (v0.3.0 == origin/main).

2. Prompt enhancer disabled: inspect.signature(ErnieImagePipeline.__call__)
   against the real installed diffusers confirms use_pe defaults True.
   Reading _enhance_prompt_with_pe in the installed diffusers source shows
   what it does when enabled: a SEPARATE auxiliary LLM .generate() call
   rewrites the caller's prompt before image synthesis. Left at its
   default, this would silently override paperbanana's own
   carefully-engineered prompt (its Planner/Stylist agents already do this
   work) with a second, opaque LLM rewrite. Now explicitly
   USE_PROMPT_ENHANCER = False, passed as use_pe=False on every call --
   never left to the pipeline's own default.

tests/python/test_ernie_image_server.py: 13 tests now (up from 11), all
passing -- added explicit assertions for the Turbo inference settings and
for use_pe=False, and strengthened _StubPipeline to require use_pe as an
argument (a regression guard: dropping the use_pe= kwarg from the real call
site now fails every mocked test immediately). use_pe=False and the Turbo
kwargs were independently verified to bind against the REAL
ErnieImagePipeline.__call__ signature via inspect.signature(...).bind_partial,
not just the mocked stub. ruff/ruff-format/mypy clean; manual smoke test
confirms the honest blocked_ernie_image_not_cached path still fires,
correctly naming the Turbo repo id.

Spec (REQ-PUBLISH-042/SCENARIO-PUBLISH-042), traceability, known-issues.md,
status.md, and changelog.md all updated -- original adoption text preserved
via same-day addenda, nothing silently edited, per Documentation Update
Rules.

